U(i,j)-Average     0.0306       0.0300       0.0308      -0.0006      -0.0046      -0.0132       0.0302 0.0279 0.0308 0.0319   1.14


                                                 =====================
                                      The Displacement Factor has the Form of Exp(-T)

                                                      where

                             T = 8*(pi**2)*Uiso*sin(theta/lambda)**2, for Isotropic Atoms,

  T = 2*(pi**2)*(U11*(h*as)**2+U22*(k*bs)**2+U33*(l*cs)**2+2*U23*k*l*bs*cs+2*U13*h*l*as*cs+2*U12*h*k*as*bs),for Anisotr. Atoms

                                      Ueq = 1/3 Sum(i,j) (Uij*as(i)*as(j)*a(i).a(j))

                                   U1, U2, U3 are the three Main Axes Components of Uij

Reference U(eq): R.X. Fischer & E. Tillmanns, Acta Cryst. (1988). C44, 775-776

